-- 96_quest_reference_repairs.sql -- map 751 Lordaeron extension, DB step 35.
--
-- GENERATED by Custom/Documentation/scripts/gen_map751_quest_ref_repairs.py.
--
-- The fourth class of post-import quest-validation errors: quest fields pointing at
-- things this server does not have. 68 log lines over four groups.
--
-- THREE OF THE FOUR ARE FIXED BY MAKING THE DATA HONEST, NOT BY INVENTING CONTENT.
-- Each group was traced to its source before deciding, and the reasoning is here so
-- the choice is reviewable rather than implied.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- 1. Item 68647 -- REAL FIX. The one item 94_ could not build ("absent from
--    Item-sparse"), and it blocks quest 29377 "A Time to Break Down" twice
--    (StartItem and ItemDrop2). It is not in the Cata client, but it IS in
--    nelt_world.item_template -- a full 3.3.5-format row, "Dousing Agent",
--    class 12 (Quest), displayid 55112, which our ItemDisplayInfo already has.
--    So it needs no client-side work at all.
--
--    SCHEMA TRAP: both tables have 138 columns but only 110 share a name, so a
--    SELECT * would silently misalign. The 110 are named explicitly below. The 28
--    we have and nelt does not are armor/damage/resistance/ppm fields that default
--    to 0 and mean nothing for a quest item.
--
-- 2. ZoneOrSort -- REAL FIX, by remapping to the parent zone that exists.
--      4706 = Jintha'Alor      (11 quests) -> 47, The Hinterlands
--      5287 = Darkspear Strand  (1 quest)  -> 14, Durotar
--    Both are genuine Cata AreaTable rows (confirmed in the 4.3.4 client) that
--    3.3.5 does not have. Rather than add AreaTable rows -- a DBC rebuild plus an
--    AreaBit, and they would be the only subzone sorts in the band -- they take
--    their PARENT zone. That matches the convention the rest of the import already
--    uses: every other map-751 quest sorts under a plain stock zone id
--    (47 x67, 267 x50, 45 x38, 85 x36, 130 x19 ...). 4706 was the only invalid
--    one, and 47 is where its 67 siblings already sort.
--
--    Note 28704 "Warchief's Command: The Cape of Stranglethorn!" is Durotar
--    bulletin-board content that leaked into the import and has no questgiver at
--    all. Fixing its sort clears the log line; it stays unreachable either way.
--
-- 3. RewardSpell -- SPLIT. Of the 15 missing spells, 10 exist in the Cata 4.3.4
--    client and are added to the spell downport in 88_ (now 237 spells -- RE-APPLY
--    IT). The other 5 do not exist in the 4.3.4 client AT ALL:
--        89550, 89669, 89781, 94710, 95818
--    They were removed from the game before 4.3.4, so the cata_world snapshot
--    predates its own client. There is nothing to downport. The 7 affected quests
--    get RewardSpell = 0, which is what the core already does with an invalid id --
--    this only stops it complaining. They are cosmetic / despawn-helper spells,
--    not player abilities, so nothing is lost.
--
-- 4. RewardNextQuest -- HONEST FIX, 38 chains zeroed. Every one of the 38 targets
--    exists in cata_world and has a questgiver there, so importing them was
--    considered and rejected: NOT ONE of those questgivers has a spawn on map 751,
--    and 30 of the 38 do not exist in our creature_template at all. They live in
--    Orgrimmar (Grezz Ragefist, Ormak Grimshot, Zevrost, Master Pyreanor, Sunwalker
--    Atohmo, Shadow-Walker Zuru ...), Moonglade (Loganaar), Ragefire Chasm and
--    Stranglethorn. These are Cata "now report to your class trainer" follow-ups --
--    capital-city content, not Lordaeron content.
--
--    Importing them would have produced 38 quests nobody can pick up, and grafting
--    Cata quests onto stock Orgrimmar NPCs is exactly what this project does not do
--    (the same reason 92_ leaves 337 shared quests alone). Zeroing is behaviourally
--    identical to today -- the core already ignores an invalid RewardNextQuest --
--    and makes the data say what is actually true.
-- ============================================================================

